        "original_id": "87f50bb0-b07f-5199-bbed-5c2dcfcab194",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harold Leventhal, Don McLean, Woody Guthrie, Pete Seeger, Alan Arkin, Judy Collins, Theodore Bikel, Arlo Guthrie, Joan Baez, Mary Travers, Tom Paxton\n- Roles: American music manager, American singer-songwriter\n- Organizations: The Weavers, RIAA\n- Works: \"American Pie\"\n- Concepts: Song of the Century\n\nFacts:\n- Harold Leventhal was born on May 24, 1919, and he was an American music manager.\n- Don McLean was born on October 2, 1945, and he is an American singer-songwriter.\n- Harold Leventhal managed The Weavers, Woody Guthrie, Pete Seeger, Alan Arkin, Judy Collins, Theodore Bikel, Arlo Guthrie, Joan Baez, Mary Travers, Tom Paxton, and Don McLean.\n- Don McLean is best known for \"American Pie.\"\n- The RIAA recognized \"American Pie\" as a \"Song of the Century\" and ranked it 5th out of 25.\n- \"American Pie\" is about changes in American society from the late 1950s to the early 1970s through metaphorical references to the music industry.\n- Harold Leventhal died on October 4, 2005, at the age of 86.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
